<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mac Giolla Phádraig</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as FitzPatrick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mac Giolla Phádraig, later anglicised as FitzPatrick, was the ruling dynasty of the Irish kingdom of Osraige, named after Giolla Phádraig, a 10th-century king. After the Anglo-Norman invasion they lost the lowlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> but kept lordship in upper Osraige. In 1541 Barnaby Mac Giolla Phádraig surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> and was made Baron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-ossory">Upper Ossory</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mac-giolla-phadraig.jpg" alt="Mac Giolla Phádraig" width="320" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wikimandia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fitzpatrick_of_Ossary.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
